2026-08-25T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2021) '### The merge method
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2021) '`allow_squash_merge` and `allow_rebase_merge` are both `false`, leaving
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2021) '`allow_merge_commit` as the only way a pull request can land. Auto-merge
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2021) 'stays enabled; with the other two off it can only produce a merge commit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2021) 'This is not a preference for more commits. A split costs CI linearly:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2021) 'every commit must pass on its own, so a branch of `n` commits is `n`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2021) 'verifications and not one, paid again on every push while the branch
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2021) 'lives. Against that a split buys understandability, review reads one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2021) 'idea at a time, and `git bisect` lands on a change small enough to read
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2021) 'rather than on a whole feature.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The trade is real in both directions and it is decided per branch. Most
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2021) 'branches are one idea and should be squashed locally before the pull
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2021) 'request is final; the doc-gate port in `fabric#52` was collapsed from
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2021) 'four commits to one for exactly that reason. A split earns its keep only
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2021) 'when the concerns are independent, as in `fabric#54`, where a new gate
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2021) 'and a documentation correction had nothing to do with each other and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2021) 'each passed alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2021) 'So the question the setting answers is not how many commits a branch
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2021) 'should have. It is who decides, and when:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Squashing at merge time decides for every branch, after review, and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2021) '  collapses the series that was deliberately kept along with the ones
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2021) '  that were not. The author already had the cheaper option, `git rebase
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2021) '-i` before marking the PR ready, and it costs the same CI either way,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-2021) '  because the squashed branch is verified once as one commit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-2021) '- A squash or a rebase also gives the merge a new SHA, so the branch tip
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:35Z (RFD66606-2021) '  is not an ancestor of the default branch afterwards. The documented
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:36Z (RFD66606-2021) '  post-merge check reads exactly that, and reported three complete merges
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:37Z (RFD66606-2021) '  as unmerged in a single day.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:38Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:39Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The second could be answered by comparing trees instead of commits, and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:40Z (RFD66606-2021) 'that change is worth making anyway because history already holds squashed
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:41Z (RFD66606-2021) 'merges. It does not answer the first.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:42Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:43Z (RFD66606-2021) '### Why not a merge queue
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:44Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:45Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The earlier form of this decision required a `merge_queue` rule. The
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:46Z (RFD66606-2021) 'queue serializes entries and builds each against the branch tip, which
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:47Z (RFD66606-2021) 'is worth its cost on a repo with enough concurrent PRs that rebasing by
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:48Z (RFD66606-2021) 'hand becomes the bottleneck. This repo merges documentation changes a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:49Z (RFD66606-2021) 'few at a time, and the queue charged for capacity it never used:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:50Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:51Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Every merge needs an explicit enqueue step, and the queue snapshots
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:52Z (RFD66606-2021) '  the PR head at enqueue time, so a late fix races the merge and can be
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:53Z (RFD66606-2021) '  orphaned.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:54Z (RFD66606-2021) '- `gh pr merge --delete-branch` fails while a queue is enabled
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:55Z (RFD66606-2021) '  ("Cannot use `-d` or `--delete-branch` when merge queue enabled"), so
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:56Z (RFD66606-2021) '  branch cleanup has to move to the repo-level
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:57Z (RFD66606-2021) '  `delete_branch_on_merge` setting.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:58Z (RFD66606-2021) '- The `merge_queue` rule names no CI job on its own. A ruleset carrying
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:59Z (RFD66606-2021) '  `pull_request` + `merge_queue` and no `required_status_checks` rule
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:00Z (RFD66606-2021) '  merges a PR through the queue even when every check on it failed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:01Z (RFD66606-2021) '  This bit two dependent repos (`taskweft/taskweft`, `taskweft/nif`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:02Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:03Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The strict `required_status_checks` policy keeps the property the queue
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:04Z (RFD66606-2021) 'was there for, a change is tested against the tip it joins, and the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:05Z (RFD66606-2021) 'enqueue discipline goes away with it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:06Z (RFD66606-2021) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:07Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:08Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Good: `main` only changes through PRs, and a PR behind the tip
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:09Z (RFD66606-2021) '  updates and re-runs its checks before it lands.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:10Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Good: the configuration is captured here and reproducible from the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:11Z (RFD66606-2021) '  ruleset JSON.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:12Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Good: merging is a single `gh pr merge` with no enqueue step and no
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:13Z (RFD66606-2021) '  dequeue-to-fix dance.
 # tags: rfd:details
